{"title":"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a square. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc7892b9acc4ec136a9946aadb6c0f15ff1ed41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> respectively<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d198e115ee5481f6012df3f623690b4bcab5f869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"4\" height=\"5\" /> such that the areas of quadrilaterals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015d743b987757e68b3358948547834d9c9c5ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc8abfc0be96c3f3ca5a5d69d467418c4bc6145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BPQC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/f/0ef9ca64d92c34ac479e415fd7a4a0bf81d19028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> respectively. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34fd1dcdcfd435f8ba57e8cdee8f462bffb7af79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{AP}{BP}=2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"62\" height=\"21\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9f76ca445cb36e79515aa58c06bf83fc58b27d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{DQ}{CQ}=\\tfrac{a}{b},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"65\" height=\"24\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e67c0930c74ea344606d3c8ea9f42444338435.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import geometry;  point B = (0,0); point C = (16,0); point A = (0,16); point D = (16,16); point P = A * 1/3; point Q = C * 38/85 + D * 47/85;  // Square ABCD draw(A--B--C--D--A); dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,NW); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,SW); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,SE); dot(D); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,NE);  // Segment PQ draw(P--Q); dot(P); label(&quot;P&quot;,P,W); dot(Q); label(&quot;Q&quot;,Q,E);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n</p><p>From the problem, we know that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/089e05f7fcb8c9233b12f876225f7313346a9cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCD]=[APQD]+[BPQC]=20+21=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"377\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, the side length of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665a8f186db8a9dcbb014dce96f21db235952eeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />. Furthermore, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd59023564a68bb5e2f147ec30e18e2c73d3d52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{AP}{BP}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"60\" height=\"23\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8b0991da6ca80333fe0522a4eb7ad892ff27bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = \\tfrac{2}{3}\\sqrt{41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"98\" height=\"26\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5e0a64bcbb8e452f3263d49309271426fc8e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DQ} \\parallel \\overline{AP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"22\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015d743b987757e68b3358948547834d9c9c5ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> is a trapezoid. Thus, if we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e7847a6aa2e82b91dc00fa2e6e50e0404d2d5e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015d743b987757e68b3358948547834d9c9c5ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28a6342151fa62227d17c76e1b37b41b121fbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+\\tfrac{2\\sqrt{41}}{3}}{2}*\\sqrt{41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"46\" />. Equating this to the given area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we can now solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{x+\\tfrac{2\\sqrt{41}}{3}}{2}*\\sqrt{41} &amp;= 20 \\\\\n\\frac{\\sqrt{41}x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{3}*\\sqrt{41} &amp;= 20 \\\\\n3\\sqrt{41}x+82 &amp;= 120 \\\\\nx &amp;= \\frac{38}{3\\sqrt{41}} = \\frac{38\\sqrt{41}}{123}\n\\end{align*}\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/30001596782d6a6b2e974b973a2633eb6f746f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CQ=\\sqrt{41}-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"23\" />, we can now find a value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d0fa8ef8558d2c82e57a8ff3d11b118f8b55e7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DQ}{CQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"36\" height=\"43\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{DQ}{CQ} &amp;= \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{41}-x} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{\\tfrac{38\\sqrt{41}}{123}}{\\sqrt{41}-\\tfrac{38\\sqrt{41}}{123}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{38}{123-38} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{38}{85}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7324488561ec7bbd0c4d817859bb93a58b8859e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38+85=\\boxed{123}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I\" title=\"2021 CIME I\">2021 CIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2021\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 CIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CIME Problems and Solutions\"> All CIME Problems and Solutions</a>